{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_691526d72d861e51\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_691526d72d861e51/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"QN rule version reconciliation\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088\", \"member_8fa4d06e2bbd02e4e0e07a2a\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that the help page still lists an old quarantine trigger and asks whether a later announcement replaces the older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks which safety quarantine rule applies after the previous week's change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors, one in each thread, ask that the local clarification be followed for the case and say the conflicting QN documents still require version reconciliation before a general policy update; these are participant requests, not authoritative instructions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions say clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN, require checking that no real individual is identifiable, and explicitly replace only the older help page's blanket fictional-contact trigger. Actual identifiable private information still requires review; ambiguous details or separate QN triggers require retaining evidence for review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ confirms that the dated fictional-placeholder clarification supersedes the blanket fictional-contact trigger in QN help page v1.0, states that the older copy has not been rewritten, and directs reporting that stale copy for correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval record records approval of documentation and communication work, with document updates still pending and no observed outcome at approval; it does not establish publication or a standing rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 18 follow-up records partial completion: the instructions contained the scoped rule, the FAQ named the supersession, an announcement had been posted, and QN help page v1.0 still contained blanket initial-quarantine wording. It records remaining correction work, not an unresolved general rule or a later repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead's October 2 batch announcement notes old QN criteria remaining in a help page and asks for examples in its thread while scope is checked; that directive concerns example collection, not a replacement quarantine rule or an escalation route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether a later announcement replaces the old QN trigger; a tutor asks which quarantine rule applies after a recent change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance settles the fictional-contact exception and identifies the older help-page wording as stale and needing correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in each thread asks the thread starter to follow a local clarification while saying the conflicting documents still need reconciliation before a general policy update.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current instructions exempt clearly fictional contact placeholders alone, require checking that no real individual is identifiable, and preserve review for ambiguous details or separate QN triggers.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier follow-up records that the instructions and FAQ reflected the clarification, but the older help page still contained the blanket initial-quarantine wording.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The batch announcement asks for examples in its thread while scope is checked; it does not direct a change to the quarantine rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current FAQ explicitly identifies the stale copy and calls for correction. Repairing that reference addresses the documented conflict without reopening the settled, narrowly scoped rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): The older help-page trigger remains identified as stale while a QA tutor and a tutor ask which rule applies, supporting correction of the conflicting reference now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\\". The announcement concerns the same batch and stale QN criteria. Its directive governs where examples are collected, not which quarantine rule applies or where issues must be escalated.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: A QA tutor receives a case-specific request to follow a local clarification, but the reply does not answer whether the later announcement replaces the older note and still describes reconciliation as needed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_8fa4d06e2bbd02e4e0e07a2a\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_8fa4d06e2bbd02e4e0e07a2a is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: A tutor receives a case-specific request to follow a local clarification, but the reply does not spell out the applicable quarantine rule and still describes reconciliation as needed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: Questions in two threads concern which safety quarantine rule governs, rather than a cosmetic documentation problem. The evidence supports contained uncertainty about handling, but does not show bypassed controls or widespread task disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[0]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\\\": A QA tutor asks whether a newer announcement replaces an old quarantine trigger, and a tutor separately asks which quarantine rule applies after a change; both questions concern safety handling.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:correct_help_page\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Update the documentation. Instruction: Correct the older QN help page's fictional-contact branch to match the current instructions, preserving review for identifiable private information and separate triggers. Draft to copy: Contact details: Clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN. Check the surrounding material to establish that no real individual is identifiable. Actual identifiable private information still requires review. If details are ambiguous or a separate QN trigger exists, retain the evidence for review.\\n\\nThe September 10 fictional-placeholder clarification replaces the older blanket fictional-contact trigger only. It does not replace unrelated safety controls. Do not extend the fictional-placeholder exception beyond its scope. Use the current Safety Classification instructions and FAQ for this scoped clarification. Why this helps: The current FAQ explicitly identifies the stale copy and calls for correction. Repairing that reference addresses the documented conflict without reopening the settled, narrowly scoped rule. Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): The older help-page trigger remains identified as stale while a QA tutor and a tutor ask which rule applies, supporting correction of the conflicting reference now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:post_scoped_alignment\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a scoped clarification in both question threads that explains the fictional-placeholder exception and directs examples to the batch announcement thread. Draft to copy: For the fictional-contact question, the current Safety Classification instructions and FAQ replace only the older blanket fictional-contact trigger. Clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN, but check the surrounding material to establish that no real individual is identifiable. Actual identifiable private information still requires review. If the details are ambiguous or another QN trigger applies, retain the evidence for review. This does not change unrelated safety controls. Please keep examples in the batch announcement thread while the scope check continues. Why this helps: A direct reply gives the tutors the narrow rule that their existing replies do not spell out and preserves the requested place for examples. It can clarify handling promptly, but leaves the conflicting help-page wording in place. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Two current questions ask which quarantine rule applies, and the replies refer to local clarification without stating the supersession established by the current instructions and FAQ.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:observe_existing_scope_check\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"No action needed now. Instruction: Defer an additional post or documentation edit while observing the existing batch scope check. Draft to copy: No additional post or documentation edit is proposed now; leave the existing example collection and scope check in place. Why this helps: Observation is plausible because the team lead is already checking scope and local replies exist. However, the announcement does not require waiting on the narrow correction, and the current FAQ explicitly calls for the stale copy to be reported for correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088\", \"thread_id\": \"1790862407.000075\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_r